  "term": "IDS",
  "definition": "In this context, IDS refers to the Inventory of Depressive Symptomatology Self-Report, a self-report measure used to evaluate mood disorders. The source specifically discusses its use in older adults with subjective cognitive decline and mild cognitive impairment.",
